interfaces = []
do_1 = "In services/explorer/backend/apps/indexer/lib/indexer/fetcher/paxeer_x/price_acceptance_replay.ex:52 handle database query failures locally around the held_jobs diagnostic at line 56, report diagnostic unavailability explicitly and return usable replay state so the step result at line 35 still controls the normal completion, batch interval and bounded error retry at lines 38-48; do not convert a failed query into an empty held-job result or suppress errors from the replay step, and preserve the successful count, lowest block, error and warning throttle at lines 55-59."
do_2 = "Extend services/explorer/backend/apps/explorer/test/repair/repair_22_31_490_test.exs:119 with declared regression functions replay_database_outage_recovers and replay_held_warnings_survive_database_outage registered through ExUnit tests: use the real PriceAcceptanceReplay, PriceAcceptanceBackfill and PostgreSQL query path with temporary database query unavailability and guaranteed restoration, without test doubles; cover startup with last_held_warning_at nil and a subsequent outage when the diagnostic is due, monitor the original runner and backfill worker for survival, assert retries respect the configured interval without a restart loop, then restore query availability and prove timer-driven replay resumes and completes without manually sending replay."
do_3 = "In those regression tests assert durable queue and observation state is preserved during each outage and advances correctly after recovery, and capture a successful held-job diagnostic after availability returns to assert count, lowest block and error remain useful and warnings are still limited to once per minute; preserve the existing assertions at services/explorer/backend/apps/explorer/test/repair/repair_22_31_490_test.exs:125 and line 166."
